    "body": "- [ ] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n# What does this PR do?\n\nPreserve the recursive path in `diff()` when a list, tuple or NumPy array has extra elements.\n\nFor example:\n\n```python\nfrom megatron.core.dist_checkpointing.dict_utils import diff\n\ndiff({\"layers\": [[1, 2, 3]]}, {\"layers\": [[1]]}, prefix=(\"checkpoint\",))\n```\n\nCurrently `only_left` is `[2, 1]`, losing the enclosing keys and index. This returns\n`[(\"checkpoint\", \"layers\", 0, 2), (\"checkpoint\", \"layers\", 0, 1)]` instead, matching\nthe path contract already used for dictionary keys and value mismatches.\n\n`_validate_common_state_dict()` uses these paths when reporting rank-to-rank\ncheckpoint differences. Missing-element ordering and value comparison behavior\nare unchanged. No training, numerical or performance behavior is changed.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Added eight parametrized unit cases covering both directions, list/tuple/array,\n  nested and root paths, empty sequences, and ordinary value mismatches.\n- Supplemental native-package CPU probe: six nested-path checks failed before\n  the fix and passed afterward; three equality/dictionary/mismatch controls passed\n  in both arms (Torch 2.12.0+cpu, CUDA hidden). This is not the distributed CI suite.\n- Ran the unmodified `tools/autoformat.sh` in check mode against a private Linux\n  snapshot: Black, isort, Pylint and Ruff passed; the script exited 0. Mypy reported\n  six errors on unchanged lines outside this fix and is nonblocking in that script.\n- The repository's distributed unit suite has not been run locally; CI is pending.\n- The commit is SSH-signed and DCO-signed-off. GitHub signing-key registration is\n  pending (`unknown_key`), so this stays Draft rather than claiming CI readiness.\n\n## Contribution pre-checks\n\n- [x] I have added relevant unit tests.\n- [x] I have run `tools/autoformat.sh` on my PR.\n- Functional training tests and kernel determinism changes are not applicable to\n  this diagnostic-only fix.\n\nThe personal-review checkbox above is left for the human author; it is not an\nautomated-review claim.\n",
